--[[
================================================================================

        D O O R S   D U M P

        Run it INSIDE a DOORS run, IN ROOM 0 -- before you open the first
        door. Nothing can hunt you there, and parts of this take a while.

        It writes everything needed to understand the game into a NEW folder
        in your executor's workspace, named with the date and time -- so it
        can never overwrite an older dump, which is exactly how the last
        DOORS dump got lost.

            loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/main/DoorsDump"))()

        STAND STILL until the caption says it is done. The first 8 seconds are
        the FPS measurement, then about 25 seconds of testing four graphics
        levels. Walking into a new room would measure the room loading
        instead of the game running.

        The graphics test changes the level for THIS SERVER ONLY and puts it
        back when it is finished. Nothing is saved.

        WHAT IT WRITES
        --------------
            report.txt        FPS over 8 seconds (average, 1% and 5% low,
                              stutters) and where each frame's time goes,
                              memory by type, ping, your graphics settings,
                              every Lighting property and effect, and a cost
                              census of each room: parts, shadow casters,
                              lights, shadowed lights, particles, highlights
            graphics_sweep.txt  FPS, frame times and draw calls at graphics
                              1, 4, 7 and 10 -- whether max graphics can
                              ever run on this PC, measured instead of guessed
            tree_*.txt        the instance tree of ReplicatedStorage, your
                              PlayerGui (MainUI -- the modifiers bar lives
                              there), PlayerScripts, Lighting and the rooms
            modules/          the source of every client script the game has
                              loaded, if your executor can decompile

        The report is written FIRST, before the slow parts, so if decompiling
        crashes the game you still keep the numbers.

================================================================================
]]

local Players           = game:GetService("Players")
local RunService        = game:GetService("RunService")
